## What actually moves in the window
MonumentCount -0.46 -> -0.13 -> +0.91 -> +0.35 -> -0.36 ; AxesCelts 0.37 -> 0.32 -> 2.60 -> 0.80 -> 0.80
(both peak 3200 BCE). HouseSize 2.05 -> 0.79 -> 0.79 -> -0.06 -> 0.19 (its step down happens 3400->3300 BCE).
Depot -0.45 -> -0.43 -> -0.29 -> -0.37 -> -0.37 (small absolute range 0.16 Z, same 3200 BCE peak).
Belau openness 1.65 -> 2.10 -> 0.75 -> 0.33 -> -1.16 (declining); KDE find density 4.31 -> 2.98 (x1e-4, declining).

## Covariates
House Size correlates +0.93 with kde_all_mean in-window -> its trajectory is partly observation/dating density.
Partial r (target ~ HouseSize | covariate): | Belau openness: MC -0.441 (p = 0.455), AX -0.039 (0.901);
| kde_all_mean: MC -0.172 (0.777), AX +0.367 (0.636); | g_all_mean: MC -0.525 (0.347), AX -0.155 (0.818).
Woserin PC1 moves with Belau (r = 0.78) - no site-idiosyncrasy, not used for inference.

## EN/MN boundary sensitivity (3400 BCE bin)
Dropping the 3400 BCE bin (MN-only core, N = 4) flips the sign of both target~symbolic correlations:
MC~HouseSize -0.352 -> +0.270 ; AX~HouseSize -0.166 -> +0.368. Depot, CopperGold, MonumentSize, Pottery
and the two targets' mutual correlation are sign-stable. House Size's maximum sits exactly on the EN->MN
transition (3600 BCE -1.35 -> 3500/3400 BCE +2.05), so the level association is a boundary artefact.

## Caveats
N = 5 bins (N = 4 for changes; minimum attainable exact two-sided p = 0.008 and 0.040 respectively);
2 of 3 symbolic-capital elements carry no in-window information; composite is House Size by construction;
no inference from the yearly linear-interpolated grids (effective N still 5); a single significant cell
(Depot x AxesCelts p = 0.041) is expected by chance among ~48 tests and is economic, not symbolic, capital.
